ence (REQ-AGT-103), so the resumed verifier is refused, never VERIFIED; outside an operation a provider's Retry-After was not carried across a restart (a production defect, fixed in PR #471: the interruption records `providerEligibleAt` and a resumed turn waits it out; test `cli/test/provider_wait_resume.test.ts`) |
 | A2 | P1 | Build/typecheck overlay carries only recognised source extensions (JSON/Go/C/CSS candidate edits ignored; `build.rs` overlaid) | WP-1302 | FIXED with limits (WP-1302, `cli/test/code_evaluators_overlay.test.ts`). Deviation from the plan wording ("carry every candidate build input, or fail closed and report ignored changed paths"): the overlay carries an allowlist of source and data file types and pins or ignores the rest, always reporting those paths in `details.ignoredCandidateChanges` (shell scripts, Gradle/Maven/Ruby files, symlinks, and build and checker configuration pinned by one policy: unambiguous names at any depth, and tool configs and build scripts at the project or package root only, so ordinary source such as `src/build.ts` or `src/config/database.config.ts` is carried); it does not fail closed. Not covered: a script in a carried language that the build invokes (e.g. `scripts/check.js`) is still carried and editable; candidate-produced outputs in carried types (`dist/*.js`) are carried; `node_modules/` and `__pycache__/` are skipped unreported, and `.venv/`, `.mypy_cache/`, `.pytest_cache/` and Cargo `target/` are skipped and are reported in `ignoredCandidateChanges` whenever the baseline and the candidate disagree about skipping them (a marker file confirms each); tool configs are pinned only at the project root or at a package root named by the baseline's `package.json` workspaces, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, Cargo workspace members or `go.work` (a layout no manifest declares has its nested tool configs carried as ordinary source); a very large other directory still makes the evaluator fail closed. Duplicates `01M6KXHHGA28`, `01M6KXTK3FYQ` and the section B overlay rows |
