-| A4 | P2 | Specialist contracts: `maxContextTokens` unused, `validateSpecialistOutput` has no runtime caller, required inputs are prompt advice, verdict gate covers reviewer units only | WP-1316 (new) | FIXED in WP-1316 (PR #428): ceiling at admission (`contextBudgetFailure`, source `role-ceiling`), required inputs checked before inference (`specialistInputFailure`), results validated by `classifySpecialist` with raw rejected output kept on `unit.rejectedOutputs`; all tested through `AgentWorkUnitExecutor.run` in `cli/test/specialist_contract_enforcement.test.ts`. The verdict-gate clause is partly WITHDRAWN: `isReviewRole` already covers `reviewer` and `acceptance_reviewer` (characterisation test added); `security_reviewer` has no verdict contract and now gets the structured-result gate. Operator remedies that can clear each block: `set_inputs` (JSON note) and `replace_task` decisions; `/team` takes quoted and `@file` input values. DEFERRED: `security_reviewer`/`failure_debugger` inputs are not auto-collected by the runner (supplied via `inputs`, or `name=@file` on `/team`). |
+| A4 | P2 | Specialist contracts: `maxContextTokens` unused, `validateSpecialistOutput` has no runtime caller, required inputs are prompt advice, verdict gate covers reviewer units only | WP-1316 (new) | FIXED in WP-1316 (PRs #428 and the auto-inputs follow-up): ceiling at admission, required inputs enforced before inference, specialist results validated with raw rejected output kept, remedies (`set_inputs`, `replace_task`) that clear each block. The runner now collects `security_reviewer` (`unified_diff`, `authorized_scope`) and `failure_debugger` (`failure_log`, `reproduction_command`) inputs itself from operation and workspace state, under the `/team @file:` protected-path (read_file policy and case-insensitive `.nexus`) and redaction rules; the diff is built from changed paths (NUL-separated, rendering options pinned, protected paths and both sides of a rename removed, literal pathspecs), never by parsing diff text, through a scratch index (base tree plus intent-to-add entries for untracked files) so an unstaged move of a protected file is detected as a rename rather than shown as a new file, and the same builder (`candidateDiff`) serves `reviewer` and `acceptance_reviewer` evidence; when any protected path changed, every added file is omitted too (a protected file moved past the similarity threshold, or copied out, could otherwise appear as a new file), and independently of git's heuristics an added file is also omitted when it equals a protected file present in the workspace (tracked, untracked or ignored) or shares a significant line (trimmed, non-comment, 8+ characters) with one, which covers `cp .env notes.txt`, a copy of an untouched tracked protected file (name-status runs with `--find-copies-harder`) and a partial copy past the similarity threshold (files in `.nexus` compare by exact content only; protected sources over 4 MiB or 64 MiB in total make every added file omitted); the stated limits, where credential redaction is the only guard, are lines pas